-- title:
--   Toric points lift to A-sections with torus special point
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and assume $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime p`, that is, $p$ is a nonunit of $A$, and write $\kappa_A =$ `ResidueField ↥A`. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData N₀ p A`, so in particular $\Lambda$ provides a structure morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` with `barPt A ≫ σA = genPt p`, a scheme over `base p` with a relative group law and parametrisations of its generic and special points by $J_0(N_0)$-classes, and assume $\Lambda$ satisfies `IsJacobian` (the conjunction of the abelian-scheme property bundle, commutativity of the group law, additivity and Galois equivariance of the generic and special point parametrisations, compatibility of reduction of points, and existence of Hecke endomorphisms; summarised here). Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`, with structure morphism $g \colon G \to$ `base p`, group law, bijection `O.pts` from $J_0(N_0p) =$ `JZero (N₀ * p)` (degree-zero divisor classes of the level-$N_0p$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) onto the sections of $g$ over `genPt p`, the smoothness, separatedness, finite-type, quasi-compactness, surjectivity and fibrewise preconnectedness conditions, additivity, Galois equivariance and Hecke compatibility of `O.pts`, flatness and surjectivity of multiplication by each positive integer, properness of the generic fibre, a toric rank `O.toricRank`, and the remaining recorded data including the morphism `O.torusFibre` from the split torus of rank `O.toricRank` over $\kappa_A$ to the base change of $g$ along `resPt A ≫ Λ.σA`. Let $m > 0$ and let $x$ lie in `O.toricPts m`, the subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)$ generated by the range of the family `O.toricPoint m hm`. Then there is a section $s$ of $g$ over $\sigma_A$, i.e. $s \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to G$ with $s$ followed by $g$ equal to $\sigma_A$, such that the point `(O.pts x).1` of $G$ equals `barPt A` followed by $s$, and there is a $\kappa_A$-point $y$ of the rank-`O.toricRank` split torus over $\kappa_A$ (a section of `torusStr (ResidueField ↥A) O.toricRank` over the identity) such that $y$ composed with `O.torusFibre` equals the point of the special fibre obtained from $s$ by precomposition with `resPt A` and passage to the fibre via `toFibrePt`.
--
--   This is the statement that toric points of $J_0(N_0p)$ of order dividing $m$ extend to $A$-valued sections of the Néron object at $p$ whose specialisations lie in the split toric part of the special fibre. It feeds the analysis of the Frobenius and Hecke action on the toric part, being cited by [`ModularCurve.jZeroNeronObjectAtP_smul_mem_toricPts_and_heckeGen_smul_eq_and_smul_heckeGen_eq_of_isFrobeniusAt_of_ne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jZeroNeronObjectAtP_smul_mem_toricPts_and_heckeGen_smul_eq_and_smul_heckeGen_eq_of_isFrobeniusAt_of_ne), and it relies on the description of `O.toricPts m` as the image of the character-indexed family `O.toricPoint m hm`.
